From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000020 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 23:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vtest: log the modifier the driver actually chose
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The [remora-alloc] line printed *out_modifier one statement BEFORE
*out_modifier = chosen.drmFormatModifier, i.e. the caller's stale
in-value — which is 0 on every path. So every allocation logged as
mod=0x0, and bd remora-e5x.30's host-side survey concluded "everything
is handed out LINEAR" from what was actually uninitialized memory. The
allocator's own comment says the opposite is the point: the non-linear
path deliberately picks the driver's block-linear modifiers because
NVIDIA's EGL treats LINEAR dmabufs as external-only.

Log after chosen is read, and log chosen itself. The import-refusal
correlation this line exists for is only as good as the modifier it
prints.
---
 vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c | fixed ordering
 1 file changed
diff --git a/vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c b/vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c
index 1d0e775c..3d562afa 100644
--- a/vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c
+++ b/vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c
@@ -530,12 +530,15 @@ vtest_gpu_alloc_image(uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t drm_format,
       goto out;
 
    *out_stride = (uint32_t)layout.rowPitch;
+   *out_modifier = chosen.drmFormatModifier;
    /* remora: pair this with the render server's "refused import" line. When a
     * guest import asks for more than we allocated, these two logs are the only
-    * way to see WHICH side computed the larger geometry (bd remora-e5x.30). */
+    * way to see WHICH side computed the larger geometry (bd remora-e5x.30).
+    * AFTER chosen is read: this line used to print the caller's stale in-value
+    * for the modifier, which reported every allocation as mod=0x0 and had the
+    * host side wrongly cleared of block-linear involvement. */
    vkr_log_alloc_geometry(width, height, drm_format, (uint32_t)layout.rowPitch, reqs.size,
-                          *out_modifier);
-   *out_modifier = chosen.drmFormatModifier;
+                          chosen.drmFormatModifier);
    *out_size = reqs.size;
    *out_fd = fd;
    ret = 0;
